BITS SCHOOL OF MANAGEMENT
                                  Term 4, Block 23, 2025 - 26
                                              Course Outline

Course Title: Technology in Operations

Faculty: Prof. Saravanan Kesavan and Prof. Probal Mojumder

Dates: Aug 25- Sept 7, 2025

Contact details: saravanan.kesavan@bitsom.edu.in ; probal.mojumder@bitsom.edu.in

Academic Associate: Mohd. Juned

Contact details: mohd.juned@bitsom.edu.in

Office Hours: By prior appointment only

Course Description:
A number of forces are shaping the business landscape today. The Great recession of 2007- 2009 affected the
fortunes of countless people and companies. Globalization and offshoring shifted the way companies structured their
supply chains. Demographic changes are also causing significant changes in the way products and services are
consumed. But if there is one change that trumps all the above in terms of impact on business, it is Technology.
Technology impacts businesses more because they remove constraints and create exciting new opportunities for
companies. With the change in technology, it has become necessary for companies to change their outlook on
everything from hiring, capability development, and underlying processes. In other words, the entire business model
may need to be changed. In this course, we will examine the capabilities, processes, and technologies to cost-
effectively meet customer demand.

Key Takeaways: This course will examine various new developments in technologies spanning across multiple
industries and the application of operations management principles to these developments. The topics covered in the
course include ecommerce, network effects, demand forecasting, logistics and distribution, last mile delivery, labor
issues in an on-demand economy, and software development through crowdsourcing. Case studies cover large
companies as well as startups.

Course Materials:
Required Readings: Case studies as shown in the individual class session.

Assessment:

Class Participation 35% (Attendance 10% + Class Contributions 25%)
Individual Case Write-ups & Plant Visit Writeup: 15% + 15% = 30%
Final Project 35%

Individual write-ups
You should submit a 1 page write up of the discussion questions for three of the following five eligible case studies
we cover in this class: a) Authbridge; b) 3D Systems; c) Coats; d) Uber; and e) Flashion

You do not need to write more than 3-4 sentences for each question. Write-ups should be submitted online by 08:29
AM on the day of the class (before class meets). Late submissions will not be accepted. There is no way to catch up
if you miss submitting the three writeups.

Individual assignments are given grades of one, two, or three stars. If you like, you may think of this scale as “good,
better, best”. I will be happy to provide detailed feedback so feel free to stop by and chat if you need more
information. You can discuss the cases with classmates as much as you would like, but the write-up should be your
own work.

Final Project (Teams of 5-6; students pick their groups)
Your final project would be a detailed case study capturing the past, and (your predictions of the) future of an
industry (retail, media, manufacturing, etc.) that could be impacted by a particular technology (blockchain, cloud
computing, virtual reality, autonomous driving vehicles).
Pick ONE industry and ONE technology only.
In the past section of your project, you should articulate how the old business model created and captured value. In
the future section, you need to be creative and explain how this new technology will impact the future operations of
the company/industry.
You need to present a process flow diagram before and after digitalization.

There are two deliverables for the final project: presentation slides in PowerPoint (in-class presentation) and a
report.
Your final report should not exceed 7 pages (double-spaced) but can include as many tables and figures in the
Appendix as you want. Each team should prepare a crisp presentation with about 5 slides. To ensure sufficient
variation, I will not assign the same industry-technology combination to more than one group. First-come-first-
served so email me once you have decided what you want to study. Here are some possible industries: retail,
manufacturing, transportation, media, banking, and healthcare. Here are some possible technologies: blockchain, 3D
printing, autonomous cars, virtual reality, cloud computing, etc. I am open to other industries and technologies so
check with me.

Some examples:
a) Impact of blockchain technology on supply chains
b) Impact of autonomous driving on the transportation industry
c) The Authbridge and Sunbelt case studies are good examples we covered in class (though they are about individual
companies rather than an industry).

In the report you need to have the following sections:
a) Previous workflow or process flow
b) How does digitalization affect the process flow? What are the impacts on throughput rate (TR), throughput time
(TT), and assets?
c) Does technology improve TT, TR, or assets through improved accuracy, speed, better resource allocation, or
other mechanisms?
d) What is the human impact of technology? Will the technology automate or augment work? If so, how?
e) Is a win-win-win-win strategy possible for the employers, employees, customers, and vendors with the adoption
of the technology?

Clearly, there will be much more to think about than what you can squeeze into the report so pick the salient
changes and discuss them. Your emphasis should be on the way the “operations” are impacted by this technology.
You should form your groups of 5-6 students and email the academic associates, the group members, and the topic
area before the beginning of the third class.

