Course Outline
Course Title: Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) Management
Faculty: Srinivas Pingali, Srinivas Atreya, Sirisha Peyyeti, Shankar Prakash, Jyothi Korem
Dates: 26-10-2026 to 08-11-2026; 18-01-2026 to 31-01-2026
Contact details: srinivas.pingali@bitsom.edu.in
Academic Associate: ______   Contact details: ______
Office Hours: TBD

Course Description:
This is comprehensive course on Forward Deployed Engineer Management. A Forward Deployed Engineer is a professional embedded within a client-facing or pre-sales function of an AI software company or enterprise AI team. Unlike a solutions architect (who advises) or a software engineer (who builds internally), the FDE simultaneously does both — in front of, and in service of, paying clients.

The FDE role was pioneered by companies like Palantir, where forward-deployed engineers became legendary for their ability to parachute into client organizations and deliver working software within days. The model has since been adopted by leading AI-native companies including Anthropic, Scale AI, Cohere, and others. The role has three defining characteristics:

Technical depth: The FDE must be able to build, debug, architect, and explain AI-powered systems in real time — not just on a whiteboard. Key is to be able to create PoC’s in real time to demonstrate business value.
Commercial ownership: The FDE owns the client relationship, the success metrics, and often the renewal or expansion of the commercial contract.
Consultative delivery: The FDE must translate vague business objectives into scoped, executable AI projects — and communicate progress to non-technical executives.

This course is the 1st of its kind tailored to business (MBA) students. The course combined with the AI, communication and storytelling courses will prepare MBA students for a career as FDE. Our course has module on Anthropic technologies but the learning is fungible and can be applied across any AI platforms.

Course Materials: Suggested Reading
Selling IT: The Science of Selling, Buying and Deal-making; Sandip Mukhopadhyay, Srinivas Pingali, Amitabh Satyam (Routledge 2021)
Consulting Methods: A Practical Playbook for Success; D Chakrabarti, S Rao, SR Pingali (2025)
Digital Transformation Strategies: Theory and Practice; Srinivas Pingali, Shankar Prakash, Jyothi R. Korem, Routledge (2026)

