         Dow’s Bid for Rohm and Haas (HBS)

5.   Valuation (cont’d)

         •   Nuances of DCF, considerations such as synergy, control premium that
             weigh in for final deal values (modifications to DCF)
         •   Relative valuation, how to use multiples smartly, things to look out for
         •   Tying it together – good practices followed internationally

6.   Distinctive Situations

         •   The Leveraged Buyout (LBO) and working out an LBO model (with
             caselet)
         •   Merger calculations - Merger / swap ratio and what it means through
             examples. Mergers with cross holdings.
         •   Accretion/dilution analysis

     REQUIRED
       • “The Strategic Secret of Private Equity” (Harvard Business Review)

         Case

         CoMark LBO

7.   Deal Structures – the ‘How’

         •   Different transaction themes with their characteristics & implications
         •   Should we buy /sell assets or shares
         •   Payment consideration –cash vs stock payment and implications

     We will discuss different forms like asset vs stock purchases, merger vs acquisition,
     other formats like licensing, leasing, etc. [other formats depending on time] in the
     Indian context with examples

     REQUIRED
       • Rappaport, Alfred, and Mark L. Sirower, 1999, Stock or cash? The trade-offs
